    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612-a2">

                <pb facs="1077" n="983" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg983"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 to inclosure in No.
                        157.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Valdes to Mr.
                            Springer.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">central administration of customs
                        of the island of cuba.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your attentive official
                    communication of this date regarding the present payment of tonnage dues by
                    Spanish vessels, I have the honor to inform you that in Appendix 16 of the
                    customs tariff now ruling, a copy of which was sent to your consulate, will be
                    found the tariff now ruling, together with all the regulations regarding
                    steam-ships making regular trips and mail steamers.</p>
                <p>God guard you many years.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Habana</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1886-12-15">15 December,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joaquin B Valdes.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
